[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_glm-5.1_cloud-integration-bug-trial-3[0m[0m
All 10 runs pass cleanly — no ERROR lines. All three invariants hold across every run:

- **Inventory never below zero** — stock ranges from 0 to 3 (remaining after payment failures release reservations)
- **Every charge matches a successful order** — `total_charged == successful × price` in every run
- **Zero duplicate charges** — each order_id charged at most once

### Summary of changes

**Root causes**: Two classic concurrency bugs — a TOCTOU race (check-then-act without a lock) and a charge-before-reserve ordering problem.

| File | Change | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `inventory.py` | Added `asyncio.Lock` to `__init__`; `decrement` and `increment` now acquire it | Eliminates the TOCTOU race — check-and-decrement is atomic, so concurrent coroutines can't all pass the check before any decrement |
| `checkout.py` | Reversed flow: `decrement` first, then `charge`; on charge failure, `increment` to roll back | Prevents ghost charges — inventory is reserved before money is taken; if payment fails, the reservation is released |
| `payments.py` | Added `_charged_ids` set; `charge` returns `True` without double-charging if the order_id was already charged | Idempotency guard — the same order can never produce duplicate charges |

The public interfaces of `Inventory` and `PaymentGateway` are unchanged; only internal behavior and new private attributes were added.
